config PM_TEST_LPCMP_LOOPBACK
	bool "GPIO loopback functional layer"
	select GPIO
	help
	  Drive the comparator's positive input from a GPIO and assert on the
	  comparator's actual output, instead of only inspecting CCR0.CMP_EN.

	  This is the only layer that proves a SUSPEND really stopped the analog
	  comparison rather than merely flipping a register bit, but it needs a
	  jumper wire on FRDM-MCXN947 between:

	      J2-11 (PIO1_12, gpio1 pin 12)  ->  J2-17 (PIO1_0, CMP0_IN0)

	  Same wiring as tests/drivers/comparator/gpio_loopback. Off by default so
	  that every other layer runs with no external wiring at all.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
